  "structure": {
    "block_count": 70,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Your Guide to Your 4-Month-Old's Sleep Schedule",
        "text_sha256": "85a6c8cc05516b96defe5ec619c5ece3074390858d02a72ae73409466ef485f9",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy changes, updates to sourcing, and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "afc7e839d614de2594a9746e1cec0160781f2935fd4768ba274024188e8cce19",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "4-month-old sleep schedule",
        "text_sha256": "ce01e8de9fa88625a0aaec2a0ef2bd27046d184eb869ef7c3fc6c9c732d7cb1d",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Wondering how much sleep a 4-month-old needs? Here's how to establish a sleep schedule for your baby.",
        "text_sha256": "658e37c209c1180774b92ded6fc98a54ce57cdac47e5374b1c1dd36412097b9c",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "By 4 months, you may have noticed that your baby doesn't sleep quite as much as she once did. That teeny newborn who used to nap so often? She's now more active and social, and increasingly interested in exploring the world around her. For many 4-month-olds, that means less daytime sleep and more hours logged in their cribs at night.",
        "text_sha256": "9297fc99ce45f413088de49b353d8483064cae471112fc56480231128a616e89",
        "word_count": 60
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Every baby is different, but your little one's sleep routine may start to become somewhat more predictable this month. However, the dreaded 4-month sleep regression can also appear around this time, making parents feel like they're right back in the newborn days. (Don't worry — as exhausting as it is, this stage will pass!) Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsGetting Your Baby to SleepSee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "b475ef1149b21423cde485cb87b9271a7bda9a8dc606d4fa927027216653a84a",
        "word_count": 66
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsGetting Your Baby to SleepSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "5ec390e6da0527b01316d2bd7be124be0e92150e9691a0a695feaca450fdc862",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's what you should know about your 4-month-old's sleep schedule, plus how much sleep your baby needs at this age.",
        "text_sha256": "3f5e574702123c756810f37aad3da8a3504cc36403c1e29e7dc6543f3f10a658",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "At 4 months old, most babies sleep 12 to 17 hours total (including three to four naps that last between 30 minutes to two hours) and may sleep six to eight hours overnight, though the 4-month sleep regression can cause more frequent night wakings.",
        "text_sha256": "d2eea63cad71d00bed6e02583a218b143c079d89d787f44ee4d852ca391f6572",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Routines may become more predictable, with wake windows of 75 minutes to two hours. Some parents begin sleep training at this age, using methods like Ferber, cry-it-out, or the chair method, while still offering at least one night feeding if needed.",
        "text_sha256": "7cae166571f01092782dbf1adacf27e7ca097c1ac64f4c44bea01cbf1ff9efa5",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your little one is struggling with sleep challenges, maintain a consistent bedtime routine, offer tummy time during the day to support developmental milestones, and continue putting your baby down drowsy but awake.",
        "text_sha256": "94a09afd3cecec4470cc30e9630543c0102082cfdb3f2e24cc70fe5b42fc31a9",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How much should a 4-month-old sleep?",
        "text_sha256": "12bd546ab82f455b17ccabb9da0325c5363839b0f4579ef80afbf05c7de1db9b",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A typical 4-month-old should get between 12 and 17 hours of shut-eye a day, including nighttime sleep and three or four naps. Still, every baby's sleep needs are different, and it's normal if your child snoozes a little more or less than that. Trusted SourceKidsHealth From NemoursNapsSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "d53a01bca85c68c5d444eeb42355caee945661912ecaab5032daecdc8a708c4b",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Naps",
        "text_sha256": "90cf0f1d8fbdc4ba984bd078806da98dc4333a709a8b7ee749ec136e156e06fe",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your 4-month-old has a stronger grasp on day and night now and may be able to sleep for six to eight hours overnight (although, again, this varies).",
        "text_sha256": "60bfccbdba73bda9edfc8d10eae959ed399447b50f8baa8c0523dda5dac64e10",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What's the best sleep schedule for a 4-month-old baby?",
        "text_sha256": "b9fb91a65eecc93b47579427558f2ae23635739dbe22c5f1c9134936d70a5df6",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some babies start to settle into a more predictable schedule this month, but keep in mind that the 4-month sleep regression can cause poor sleep for a period of time. Naps can last between 30 minutes and two hours, and it's also common for babies to start transitioning from four to three naps. Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusBedtime Habits for Infants and ChildrenSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "4535f2785af61de285fd9f9dff694eb57016c659847e028a78b49d83278cafee",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, MedlinePlusBedtime Habits for Infants and ChildrenSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "6a89ac291443f678060f65aece00119d9bc24b7e47d70a91633ae6ea3844765f",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Depending on how many naps your 4-month-old is taking, a typical day may look something like this:",
        "text_sha256": "06bc2d271edd6bf5b3d3d39b51dcfc25acb52e3423e165f86e15442383c11816",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Sample sleep schedule for a 4-month-old taking four naps",
        "text_sha256": "1ce8cedbe22b998c4d9baa78631ace354d91ea60559819eef3cdf29f10043cdb",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This schedule assumes your little one is awake for 75 minutes to two hours at a time and naps four times during the day. Trusted SourceThe Sleep FoundationHow Much Sleep Do Babies and Kids Need?See All Sources [4]",
        "text_sha256": "42d2dc6d00be1c4e5ac42d66d69dc7ed577b73a1d9a8fa41283ec75249c354e6",
        "word_count": 38
      },
